Ignore the title of the email for now, and let's go over some cool things
from this last week!

We had Eikaiwa at a small high school, Elder Childs and I were joined by
Elder McCord and Elder Stedler! It was pretty fun, and one of the kids is
here on a scholarship for basketball and wants to come to church. Pretty
lit =F0=9F=94=A5=F0=9F=94=A5

We also visited Jian's house for the first time and got to meet his dad,
who is super chill and used to be a Gymnast. We visited them twice in these
past two weeks, and the second time I got to give Jian's dad a back
massage. It was pretty lit.

We have done a lot of cool art finding these past couple weeks, making
watercolors and doodles and all kinds of things for people. I've had a
great time spreading around the Gospel message with art!

Lessons these past two weeks have been great; we invited our friend
Yamamoto san to Baptism and got an "I'll think about it" response, but
we're seeing growth in all of our friends! We have made plans to invite
each of them to Baptism as soon as we can, and as the spirit guides.

As for the title of my email, let me set the stage. It's 3:00 AM, and I
awake to sone scary sounds from the top bunk. Sounds like some weird
sputtering awfulness and then from the top bunk comes the rain of vomit.
Elder Childs probably kept hurling over the edge of the bunk bed for like 3
minutes straight. I was just kind of sitting there, stuck in the bottom
bunk for fear of the napalm. I avoided getting covered in throw up, but I
got some decent splash-age, but did throw away a blanket. I then got a
clothespin on my nose and got up and swept all the vomit into a dustpan
then a bag. Pretty Nasty lol. In the middle of everything a cockroach came
from nowhere and I obliterated it. My comp was ok, the night before he had
some raw squid thing and it did not agree with him. =F0=9F=98=82

I've been learning about Humility and boldness recently.

I've found it hard to be bold while feeling like I'm staying humble. How do
I balance the two?

If you have any ideas for me I'd love to hear from you!

I love everyone of you so much. You are in my prayers. Look for God's hand
in your life and you'll be surprised =F0=9F=94=A5=F0=9F=94=A5

Love you!!

Elder Killian

--0000000000000640cf064c0a8bcb
